  "smoke": {
    "keptGeneratorAnimation": true,
    "atlas": "volcano_smoke_atlas.png = the generator's materials/atmosphere.png (1024x1024 RGBA; top half cloud band, bottom half one puff)",
    "flipbook": {
      "file": "volcano_smoke_flipbook.png",
      "sheet": [
        1024,
        1024
      ],
      "frameSize": [
        256,
        256
      ],
      "frames": 16,
      "columns": 4,
      "rows": 4,
      "loopSeconds": 5.556,
      "fps": 2.88,
      "loop": true,
      "order": "row-major from the top-left",
      "alpha": "straight (not premultiplied); draw with standard alpha blending, no depth write",
      "ventAnchor": {
        "u": 0.5,
        "v": 0.1375,
        "note": "frame-relative, v measured from the bottom; put this point on the crater"
      },
      "worldSize": "the window is 0.40 x 0.40 panorama units; on a 2048x1024 panorama that is ~819 px wide, so scale the quad to the backdrop",
      "source": "port of RPGWorldBuilder/PaintedBackground.shader smoke pass (four puffs, age = frac(t*0.045 + j*0.25 + 0.04)) at smokeSpeed = 1",
      "atlas": "volcano_smoke_atlas.png is the generator's original RGBA atlas (top half cloud band, bottom half single puff) for engines that re-implement the shader"
    },
    "shaderMaths": "time t (s); for j in 3..0: age = frac(t*0.045*smokeSpeed + j*0.25 + 0.04); centre = (0.126 - 0.065*age + 0.006*sin(age*7 + t*0.18*smokeSpeed), 0.515 + 0.22*age) in panorama UV; size = (0.055 + 0.18*age, 0.065 + 0.13*age); q = (uv - centre)/size + 0.5; puff = atlas(0.008 + q.x*0.984, 0.008 + q.y*0.484); fade = smoothstep(0,0.04,age) * (1 - smoothstep(0.78,1,age)); colour = lerp(colour, puff.rgb, puff.a*fade*0.82). Clouds: atlas top half scrolled by frac(uv.x - t*0.0018*cloudSpeed).",
    "howToUse": "Simplest: a world-space quad above the backdrop crater playing volcano_smoke_flipbook.png (4x4, 16 frames, 2.88 fps, loop) with alpha blending and the ventAnchor on the crater. Or re-implement shaderMaths in a built-in pipeline shader with volcano_smoke_atlas.png. The URP shader itself is not shipped."
  },
  "deviations": [
    "The scene generator's public API (control.py v1) only produces whole scenes (village / chapter / dungeon). It has no modular-kit action, so the parts could not come out of generate directly. The official pipeline was run unchanged (capabilities -> plan -> validate -> generate -> inspect, natural volcano preset, landforms.style=volcanic_wilderness) into runs/spellduel-volcano-kit-001 to supply the generator's tile textures, the smoke atlas and the style reference; the parts themselves were built by a separate stand-alone Blender script (kit_builder.py, in the job folder) that reuses the generator's Blender, tiles and FBX conventions. No generator source file was modified.",
    "Art: parts are procedural rock (noise-displaced, decimated) textured by projecting the generator's volcanic-natural-v3 tiles and re-grading them to the ground texture's red-brown family; AO and a top-left key light are baked into the albedo. It reads as stylised low-poly rock rather than individually hand-painted sculpts.",
    "Dimensions: wall_corner_in is about 3.2 x 3.2 m in footprint (2 x 2 m filler block plus a scree pile in the player-side crease) instead of ~2 x 2; wall pieces measure about 4.3 m wide so neighbours overlap by ~0.15 m per side; gate frames are ~4.3-4.5 m wide; the cave entrance is ~13 x 9 x 7.8 m; the exit altar is 0.5 m high at the tallest pillar with a 0.3 m flat platform. Exact bounds per part are in kit.json.",
    "A single FBX per gate variant contains both objects (gate_frame, gate_door) as siblings rather than two separate files; the same applies to vent (vent_rim + vent_core).",
    "Import was verified only in a throwaway Unity 2022.3.62f2 project (axis, scale, pivot, child placement), not inside the SpellDuel Unity project.",
    "Mobile frame rate was not measured; only triangle counts and texture sizes are reported."
  ],
